"""Evidence-led TECH-06 reports. No network access."""
import json
from collections import Counter
from .build import OUT, ROOT, OLD, read, PERIODS

def report(indices,directory,global_rows,rotation,days):
    counts=Counter((r['classification'],r['in_upstox_catalog']) for r in directory)
    histories=[r for r in indices if r['daily_history_verified']]
    pending=len(indices)-len(histories)
    text=f'''# TECH-06 status — incomplete technical data block

Document Intelligence remains paused. No stock classification, financial analysis or ML work was started. Existing company classifications are reused only for the requested crosswalk.

The public Upstox Global and NSE BOD catalogs were downloaded on 4 November 2026. They contain 13 global instruments and {len(indices)} unique NSE index instruments. Catalog presence is distinct from a successful historical response.

The complete official directories inspected contain 34 sectoral, 51 thematic and 22 broad-market entries. Exact/explicitly reviewed catalog aliases match {counts['SECTORAL',True]} sectoral, {counts['THEMATIC',True]} thematic and {counts['BROAD_MARKET',True]} broad-market entries. All directory entries, including missing identities, are retained. Other catalog indices remain explicitly OTHER_UNCLASSIFIED, rather than being forced into industry groups. BSE indices were not needed for this NSE layer and were not mixed into it.

{len(histories)} NSE indices have retained successful daily responses: Nifty 50, NIFTYMIDSML400, Nifty Auto, Nifty Consumer Durables and India VIX. All five cover the retained 227-session study grid from 1 December 2025 to 30 October 2026; Nifty 50 also has earlier retained observations. Four are price indices and appear in the rotation dataset; VIX remains volatility context. Only two of the retained histories are sectoral, so sector rankings explicitly compare those two, not the entire NSE sector universe. NIFTYMIDSML400 also has three retained 5-minute response slices (3,900 bars, 17 August–30 October 2026); exact first/last candle-start timestamps and hashes are in RETAINED_INDEX_INTERVALS.csv. These are Q2/October retrospective intraday slices, not pre-open observations or complete Q4/Q1 intraday coverage.

All five have complete descriptive price grids for FY2026 Q4 (Jan–Mar), FY2027 Q1 (Apr–Jun) and FY2027 Q2 (Jul–Sep). These are fiscal price quarters; earnings announcement/checkpoint studies extend into the following quarter, with the current retained grid ending 30 October. No claim is made about November Q2 announcements or later returns. Historical publication and launch/backcalculation certification is still outstanding per index. Zero strict historical delivery-verified index histories and zero verified global minute histories were added.

{pending} current catalog indices require new authorized daily requests. The exact immutable proposal is INDEX_ACQUISITION_MANIFEST.json. It orders mapped Q2 Focus/Blue exposures first, then other sectoral/thematic indices, retaining the rest of the catalog. UPSTOX_DIAGNOSTIC_MANIFEST.json contains 28 bounded global daily/minute probes. Neither manifest has been executed. Previous TECH-05 approval covered five completed requests and is exhausted; the correction explicitly requires manifest approval for new authenticated requests. No new token was read and no authenticated request or purchase was made.

US closes: retained S&P 500 has 239 provider-bucket observations and Dow has 227. Nine S&P and eight Dow labels are US holidays. All 466 labels were audited without changing dates. Actual session mapping remains unresolved. No current exact Nasdaq Composite, CME ES or CME NQ key was found. US Tech 100 and US 30 are separately identified alternatives, never substitutes. Nasdaq Composite history was not acquired.

Capital Goods: no exact Upstox key exists in the refreshed catalog. One official 30 October close was retained from a public NSE daily-file diagnostic before the Upstox-first correction. It is date-only, post-launch descriptive evidence, not complete history or a verified decision-time feature. Automated website collection was stopped after the NSE/NSE Indices terms review. Full licensed/exported history remains required. The 15 June 2026 launch gate is preserved; pre-launch backcalculation cannot be contemporaneous evidence.

USD/INR: retained dated H10 releases remain usable only in the conservative time-bounded column (167 PREOPEN and 168 POSTCLOSE sessions). They are US noon reference observations released weekly, not FBIL rates or live Indian FX. TECH-05's field named verified_feature_value included these release bounds; TECH-06 explicitly places them in the conservative category. Original TECH-05 files remain unchanged. Upstox USDINR daily/minute history is unqueried and its fixing/spot/indicative definition unresolved.

Oil: retained Brent and WTI EIA/FRED spot observations remain retrospective. Upstox BZUSD and CLUSD keys exist, but they have no retained history or certified spot/futures/CFD/settlement definition. The pending probes test coverage before any external futures purchase is considered. No generic indicator is assigned a contract expiry.

ES/NQ/GIFT: no historical contract-identified checkpoints acquired. Generic GIFT key exists with a 120-second refresh interval; it lacks expiry/contract identity. Historical minute support is untested. External archive candidates and precise cutoff windows are retained as contingency proposals, not executed. Exact paid dataset costs remain unknown until an authorized provider quote. Zero spend is authorized.

The refreshed charts preserve stock candles, all original indicator fields, custom subsector levels/activity/breadth and original formulas. Copies add NIFTYMIDSML400 comparison and corrected selected-date context. The sector dashboard uses the existing Lightweight Charts library. Descriptive returns, Pine EMA10/20, existing subsector ratio-of-returns RS55 versus Nifty 50, RS direction and trend persistence are exported. No official-index volume, institutional-flow inference, predictive signal or same-morning afternoon fixing is constructed.

Next action: review the two bounded Upstox manifests and authorize the desired request scope. Provider definitions/session mapping and historical publication evidence are independent gates even after prices are returned. The mandatory global decision-time block is not complete.
'''
    (OUT/'TECHNICAL_BLOCK_STATUS.md').write_text(text)
    (OUT/'SOURCE_RECONCILIATION.md').write_text('''# Source reconciliation and explicit evidence changes

Priority: refreshed official Upstox catalogs → retained authorized V3 responses → new bounded Upstox manifest → external source only for inadequate identities/periods. Public metadata retrievals are in inputs/public-catalog-retrieval-escalated.json with URLs, timestamps and hashes. The first sandbox DNS failure is recorded separately. Metadata byte differences from TECH-05 are not presumed to be instrument identity changes; both snapshots are preserved.

Upstox exact global keys: ^GSPC, ^DJI, SGX NIFTY and IXIX use GLOBAL_INDEX; USDINR, BZUSD and CLUSD use GLOBAL_INDICATOR. GLOBAL_INDEX|DOW FUTURES is US 30, not ES/NQ. NASDAQCOM and Capital Goods have no confirmed catalog identities. [Official instrument schema](https://upstox.com/developer/api-documentation/instruments/) and [global announcement](https://upstox.com/developer/api-documentation/announcements/global-instruments/) distinguish refresh interval from delivery. The announcement is effective 11 May 2026: this neither proves nor disproves earlier stored history. Its historical-global description specifically lists daily/weekly/monthly, while the generic [V3 documentation](https://upstox.com/developer/api-documentation/v3/get-historical-candle-data/) supports minute requests. Historical global-minute support therefore needs an actual response, not a generic availability-table assumption. The current-day intraday endpoint cannot verify earlier study dates. V3 candle timestamps label candle START, not final trade time or publication time.

All retained US provider labels are in UPSTOX_US_SESSION_RECONCILIATION.csv. US trading-date compatibility alone does not validate a bucket. No shift, carry-forward or deduplication against guessed sessions is applied. [NYSE calendar](https://www.nyse.com/publicdocs/nyse/ICE_NYSE_2026_Yearly_Trading_Calendar.pdf) and [Nasdaq calendar](https://www.nasdaq.com/market-activity/stock-market-holiday-schedule) supply independent calendar expectations only. DST uses America/New_York, not a fixed offset. Early close on 24 December 2025 is handled independently from an actual observed close.

[FRED SP500](https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/SP500), [DJIA](https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/DJIA) and [NASDAQCOM](https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/NASDAQCOM) identify price-index daily closes (Nasdaq base 5 February 1971=100). All carry the pre-approval-required copyright tag; SP500/DJIA reproduction explicitly requires written permission. No CSV histories were downloaded. FRED's latest page update is not historical publication evidence for every observation. Request research/artifact-use permission plus vintage/publication evidence before a replacement series is integrated. No Nasdaq-100 substitution.

[Official sectoral](https://www.niftyindices.com/indices/equity/sectoral-indices), [thematic](https://www.niftyindices.com/indices/equity/thematic-indices) and [broad-market](https://www.niftyindices.com/indices/equity/broad-based-indices) directory sections were retained as browser evidence and parsed dynamically. Reviewed abbreviations are explicit in build.py; they select real catalog records. Missing directory identities have no generated keys. Directory names and provider names remain separate. India VIX is not ranked with price sectors. Thematic ESG, corporate-group, faith, factor or multi-industry concepts are not automatically pure industries.

[Capital Goods factsheet](https://www.niftyindices.com/Factsheet/Factsheet_Nifty_Capital_Goods.pdf) establishes launch 15 June 2026 and earlier base history. The single official archive diagnostic is raw/ind_close_all_30102026.csv. Its exact receipt time was not retained; only retrieval date is known, and no time is invented. It was obtained before the correction. Full history was not harvested: [NSE terms](https://www.nseindia.com/static/nse-terms-of-use) prohibit systematic automated collection; [NSE Indices terms](https://www.niftyindices.com/terms-of-use) require express written consent. A licensed/exported file from the owner or [authorized data subscription](https://www.niftyindices.com/offerings/data-subscription) can close the gap. Capital Markets is explicitly distinct.

H10: use checksummed dated release tables and retained end-of-release-day NY upper bounds. The precise publication minute remains blank. No same-day afternoon rate enters PREOPEN. [FBIL methodology](https://www.fbil.org.in/uploads/FBIL_REFERENCE_RATE_FINAL_fa318d5727.pdf) samples a random 15-minute window in 11:30–12:30 IST and publishes around 13:30 on Mumbai business days. A scheduled time is not an actual receipt. [FBIL licensing FAQ](https://www.fbil.org.in/uploads/FAQ_s_updates_30th_Nov_2023_edited_version_1def7b65bb.pdf) establishes usage restrictions; no FBIL benchmark history was harvested. RBI is a reference-rate dissemination route, not proof of a live 09:15 spot price. Previous published FBIL reference would be a separate series if acquired legitimately, never silently mixed with H10 or Upstox USDINR.

Brent/WTI: reuse retained [EIA/FRED WTI](https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/DCOILWTICO) and [Brent](https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/DCOILBRENTEU). These are spot USD/barrel observations, not settlements. EIA's [price-data explanation](https://www.eia.gov/petroleum/feature/price-comparison092012_article.pdf) describes a publication cycle, not a dated vintage attestation for the retained observations. Current prices/release schedules do not establish historical availability. Retrospective classification is retained.

[CME DataMine](https://www.cmegroup.com/market-data/real-time-and-historical-data.html) supplies historical trades/top-of-book/depth. [Databento GLBX.MDP3](https://www.databento.tech/docs/datasets/glbx-mdp3) advertises CME futures from June 2010 with event/capture timestamps. [Pricing](https://databento.com/pricing/) offers usage-based history; published subscription rates are not a quote for our exact windows. No credentials/free-credit enrollment/download was attempted. [CME roll calendar](https://www.cmegroup.com/trading/equity-index/rolldates.html) has June 2026 expiry on June 18, not mechanically June 19. Proposed rolls require definition confirmation and same-contract baselines, with no back adjustment.

[NSE IX market-feed specification](https://www.nseix.com/nseixcms/sites/default/files/inline-files/NSE_IX-MarketFeed_Level2.pdf) describes historical file products. It does not establish our 2025–2026 archive coverage or cost. Exact timestamps, exchange contract/expiry, trade/quote type, capture/publication basis and intended-use license must be quoted before acquisition. A generic GIFT candle cannot meet the contract-specific requirement.

Every descriptive numerical value is linked to a retained source/hash. Missing verified values stay blank. MARKET_DATA_PROVENANCE.csv preserves inherited columns verbatim and adds explicit timestamp-basis/category columns; conceptual 15:30 and next-midnight assumptions from TECH-05 are never promoted to actual observations or release timestamps. PREOPEN and POSTCLOSE files distinguish verified, conservative and retrospective columns. Missing/stale classifications are explicit. All verified_decision_time_value cells remain blank.
''')
